From 3cf39adaa94453125306adb9b71ab5557816c379 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:44:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 096/274] TileLang V4.1 sparse-MLA metadata: the four Triton
 metadata kernels, exact

sparse_mla._requests and _tokens and attention._chunk and _pages as TileLang
kernels with the same contracts element for element: request starts,
positions and counts; per-token request, position, slot (ring rows bounded to
a request's last ring-size rows) and visible length over the first
ceil(nt / 128) blocks; sliding-window pages, lengths and top-k lengths;
page tables with block 0 and holes as -1. Integer arithmetic only, with
Triton's truncating division. Tests compare every output with the Triton
kernels over packed steps with empty and negative-position requests,
padding, holes, ring and paged groups, draft and replay windows.

(cherry picked from commit 6fdb42e28014ad2bfdcef418c51f2c3246cca673)

